port here. It will never actually be used, because no callback is ever booked.\n\nI also updated the existing \"callback scheduled_outcome\" entry in `unresolved` to say this outcome is borrowed from the third-party close rather than stated in the documents. Nothing else in the file changed."}
{"event": "policy_compiled", "run_id": "32a3cc6e4c714c2999871d4b2a0cbebc", "pid": 124158, "time": "2026-10-10T23:12:08-0700", "elapsed_s": 249.753, "artifact": "out/ext-gv.policy.json", "bands": 1, "identity_fields": ["sec_code"], "special_cases": ["dispute", "refuse_to_talk", "human", "hardship", "restructuring", "robot", "scam", "holder_not_confirmed_yet", "change_recorded_promise", "cannot_answer"], "unresolved": [{"topic": "bands", "text": "The documents define no days-late bands; a single band covering every days-late value is used with the k-date (20th of the month after the call). The upper bound 100000 is a technical catch-all, not a document value.", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}, {"topic": "attempts", "text": "ZERO persuasion: no attempts after the today question; one no ends the call (No-PTP / No-PTP). Customer may still name an amount in bottom_line..amt_due and a valid date. floor_offered_once is left at its default although the floor is never offered (no counter offers).", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}, {"topic": "floor rounding", "text": "bottom_line = greater(min_pmt, 15% of amt_due); the documents do not say how 15% is rounded.", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}, {"topic": "paid_outcome", "text": "No paid outcome exists in the v-codes sheet; 'it was paid off and closed' is grouped with the dispute lines and closes No-PTP / No-PTP, so paid_outcome is set to No-PTP and no separate already_paid case is created. No already-paid sentence is dictated.", "doc": "sources/001-02-codes.txt"}, {"topic": "third party message", "text": "Third parties are told the customer is to call GRIMSBY VALE FINANCE on the number printed on the statement; there is no phrase field for this sentence. Third parties get no purpose, no account detail, cannot pay for the customer, no exception for family; no schema field expresses these.", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}, {"topic": "callback scheduled_outcome", "text": "Callbacks are disabled ('NO callback booking'), so the documents give no scheduled-callback outcome. Every third-party call closes NOANS / CNA, so third_party.callback.scheduled_outcome repeats that pair; it is never used because no callback is ever booked.", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}, {"topic": "Sunday vs business days", "text": "The sheet defines 'business day = every day of the week. no shutdown days.' but also says 'sun day named ... -> not recordable'. The explicit business-day definition (all seven days) is kept; whether a Sunday promise date must be refused is not settled.", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}, {"topic": "write failure sentence", "text": "After the 2nd failed write the agent must 'say it failed'; no phrase field exists for this and no words are dictated.", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}, {"topic": "create_promise field names", "text": "The API lists the amount property as 'sum' but requires 'amt'; the call sheet says item_id is what create_promise wants as product_id while the API property is item_id.", "doc": "openapi.json"}, {"topic": "transfer vs promise precedence", "text": "The documents do not say whether a transfer outcome overrides a recorded promise; default kept.", "doc": "sources/000-01-call-sheet.md"}], "audit_fixed": ["Added special case holder_not_confirmed_yet: the call sheet's rule that hello / 'go ahead' / a question does not confirm the holder (answer the question, then ask again) was not represented anywhere.", "Added unresolved entry for the internal conflict between 'business day = every day of the week' and 'sun day named -> not recordable'; kept all seven days as business days.", "Added unresolved entry for third_party.callback.scheduled_outcome, which stays empty because callbacks are disabled and the documents give no outcome for them.", "Added unresolved entry for the 'say it failed' sentence after the second failed write, which has no phrase field and no dictated words.", "Expanded the third-party unresolved entry to include the restrictions (no purpose, no account detail, no paying for the customer, no exception for family).", "Widened source spans for third_party, amounts, phrases and promise_write so they quote the sentences behind their values (prohibited words, today question, the floor stated in line 40, one per item)."], "audit_unresolved": ["No days-late bands are defined; one catch-all band with the k-date is used.", "Rounding of 15% of amt_due in bottom_line is not stated.", "No paid outcome code exists; 'paid off and closed' closes No-PTP / No-PTP, so paid_outcome is No-PTP and no already-paid sentence is dictated.", "The sentence telling third parties to have the customer call the bank, and the third-party restrictions, have no schema field.", "Callback scheduled_outcome is undefined because callbacks are disabled.", "Conflict: every day is a business day vs 'sun day named -> not recordable'.", "No words are dictated for 'say it failed' after the second write failure.", "create_promise API mismatch: property 'sum' vs required 'amt'.", "Whether a transfer overrides a recorded promise is not stated."], "defaulted_without_source": []}
